WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:06.240
In 2011, Zack Snyder's stylish, violent Sucker
Punch hit theaters and introduced audiences

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:09.840
to a cast of butt-stomping young ladies in
leather.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:15.830
With a steampunk sensibility, a complex fantasy-inside-a-dream
narrative, and memorable performances from

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:20.779
a cast of up-and-comers, it was one of the
most unique films of the year — even if

00:00:20.779 --> 00:00:22.520
critics kinda hated it.

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:26.560
But what happened to Babydoll and all her
friends after the cameras stopped rolling?

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:29.089
Here's where they all ended up.

00:00:29.089 --> 00:00:30.279
Emily Browning

00:00:30.279 --> 00:00:35.250
Some folks thought that Sucker Punch would
catapult Emily Browning to A-list superstar

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:39.960
status, but her career trajectory was still
just as oddball and eclectic as ever.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:44.280
Turns out, a typical Hollywood trajectory
is the last thing on her mind.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:48.450
She's been very picky about when and where
she shows up onscreen since Sucker Punch;

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:53.390
her most mainstream role in the past five
years was in the historical disaster flick

00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:58.570
Pompeii, but her bread and butter is the foreign
and festival circuit, where she turns up in

00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:04.380
movies that most mainstream audiences will
never even hear about, let alone see in theaters.

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:09.000
As of 2017, you're most likely to catch her
on the small screen, where she's scored a

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:13.690
prime role in the Starz adaptation of Neil
Gaiman's American Gods.

00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:17.460
She's also kept a low profile in real life
— dating a guy much less famous than she

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:23.159
is and running an eclectic Instagram account
that is as un-Hollywood as they come.

00:01:23.159 --> 00:01:24.730
Vanessa Hudgens

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:29.250
Sucker Punch was a big move away from Vanessa
Hudgens' Disney roots, and she kept moving

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:33.780
in the same direction with follow-up roles
in Spring Breakers and Gimme Shelter.

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:38.690
However, Hudgens clearly hasn't gotten the
musical theater geek entirely out of her system;

00:01:38.690 --> 00:01:44.010
a few years after her gun-slinging, grenade-throwing
turn as Blondie, she was back to belting ballads

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:46.530
as Betty Rizzo on Grease Live!

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:50.920
More recently, she's enjoy ing a starring
role on primetime TV comedy Powerless, where

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:55.880
she plays an employee at Wayne Security, developing
products to keep people safe during destructive

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:57.520
superhero battles.

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:02.159
She also keeps up with fans on Instagram,
because of course she does.

00:02:02.159 --> 00:02:03.670
Abbie Cornish

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:07.140
You've gotta love Abbie Cornish's capacity
for reinvention.

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:11.340
Before Sucker Punch, she was known primarily
as the leading lady of the period romance

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:12.340
Bright Star.

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:17.450
But just as Cornish refused to be pigeonholed
into a corseted career after that, she also

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:21.910
kept it interesting and unusual after her
leather-clad turn in Sucker Punch.

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:26.340
She's starring in Geostorm, an action flick
with Gerard Butler, working with mega-stars

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:31.370
Woody Harrelson and Frances McDormand on a
dark comedy, and speaking out in an eloquent

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:34.450
defense of the controversial film Where Hands
Touch.

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:38.319
And that's not all: Cornish is also known
to occasionally take a break from her acting

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:41.200
life to spit rhymes in her second career as
a rapper.

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:43.360
Yeah, really.

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:44.440
"Gotta spin this, hoping that I win this.

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:48.380
Shameless, blameless soul, up in this, just
got the stars as a witness.

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:51.060
Hit this, like I'm gonna miss this, wishin'."

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:52.180
Jena Malone

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:56.640
By the time she scored a role in Sucker Punch,
Jena Malone had been acting for ages, and

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:57.920
she didn't slow down afterward.

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:02.349
In 2012, she traded her leather bustier for
a long skirt and high-necked blouse on the

00:03:02.349 --> 00:03:08.319
period TV drama Hatfields &amp; McCoys; the following
year, she joined the cast of The Hunger Games:

00:03:08.319 --> 00:03:10.380
Catching Fire as Johanna Mason.

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:16.040
Malone re-teamed with Sucker Punch director
Zack Snyder in 2016 for Batman v. Superman:

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:21.060
Dawn of Justice, but her scenes as Jenet Klyburn
were deleted from the theatrical release.

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:25.400
Lately, though, Malone is less involved in
Hollywood and more interested in her new roles

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:28.340
as a mom, a photographer, and a writer.

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:34.160
The actress gave birth to her first child
with fiance Ethan Delorenzo in May 2016, and

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:39.379
she now shares thoughts, poetry, and photos
on a blog called Our Mountain Family.

00:03:39.379 --> 00:03:43.520
That's a long way from gunning down bad guys.

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:45.239
Jamie Chung

00:03:45.239 --> 00:03:49.510
Scoring a role in Sucker Punch was a major
coup for Jamie Chung, who got her start on

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:55.040
MTV's The Real World and used the show as
a launchpad into a legit acting career.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:04:00.110
Since 2011, you're most likely to have seen
her in repeat appearances on Once Upon a Time,

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:05.810
where she plays the role of Mulan — or heard
her in the role of GoGo in Big Hero 6, which

00:04:05.810 --> 00:04:08.500
she'll be reprising for the TV series, too.

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:13.090
And Chung hasn't left the action realm behind;
she's been cast as the teleporting mutant

00:04:13.090 --> 00:04:16.940
Blink in Fox's new X-Men series.

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:18.140
Carla Gugino

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:23.620
After playing a therapist-slash-dance-madam
in Sucker Punch, Carla Gugino hasn't lost

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:26.139
her taste for the dark and weird.

00:04:26.139 --> 00:04:30.050
Since then, she's held down major roles on
Wayward Pines and Californication — and

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:34.630
she's even teamed up with director Zack Snyder
for a third and fourth time, lending her voice

00:04:34.630 --> 00:04:39.810
to a Kryptonian robot, and then a Kryptonian
spaceship, in his Superman films.

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:46.139
As of 2017, she's starring in the sci-fi spectacle
The Space Between Us and a feature film adaptation

00:04:46.139 --> 00:04:49.040
of the Stephen King novel Gerald's Game.

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:50.510
Oscar Isaac

00:04:50.510 --> 00:04:55.380
Between Ex Machina, X-Men: Apocalypse, and
Star Wars: The Force Awakens, you can't go

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:59.960
to the movies these days without seeing Oscar
Isaac in some form or another — which makes

00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:05.720
him the one member of Snyder's Sucker Punch
cast who's exponentially more famous now than

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:07.120
he was in 2011.

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:11.650
Isaac was right at the start of his career
when he scored a minor role in Sucker Punch.

00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:16.760
Now, he's one of the hottest actors in Hollywood,
with half a dozen prestigious projects coming

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:17.760
down the pike.

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:23.080
But perhaps because he got so mega-famous
so fast, Isaac keeps a comparatively low profile

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:24.080
in real life.

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:28.490
He's so secretive about his private life that
there's practically an entire cottage industry

00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:34.389
dedicated to unraveling the mysteries of how
he spends his time when he's not onscreen.

00:05:34.389 --> 00:05:35.600
Jon Hamm

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:40.330
Though he kept busy with Mad Men for most
of the early 2000s, Jon Hamm was never so

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:44.540
busy that he couldn't take a moment between
seasons to show up in a movie or two — and

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:47.360
in Sucker Punch, he played a small but pivotal
role.

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:52.300
In one narrative, he's the brothel's smarmy
VIP client; in the other, he's the asylum

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:57.350
doctor who lobotomizes helpless young ladies
with a stainless steel awl.

00:05:57.350 --> 00:06:02.380
Needless to say, Jon Hamm didn't disappear
after Sucker Punch; he continued for another

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:08.080
several years on Mad Men, winning a Golden
Globe and an Emmy for his performance as Don

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:09.080
Draper.

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:13.210
Not that it's all been sunshine and daisies
for Hamm in the intervening years — his

00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:18.660
longtime relationship with Jennifer Westfeldt
ended in 2015, just a few months after Hamm

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:23.720
announced that he'd entered rehab for alcohol
addiction — but he's still as sought-after

00:06:23.720 --> 00:06:24.720
as ever.

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:30.420
Next up, look for him in Edgar Wright's hotly-anticipated
heist flick Baby Driver.

00:06:30.420 --> 00:06:31.520
Scott Glenn

00:06:31.520 --> 00:06:36.230
There's just something about Scott Glenn that
says "grizzled badass" — which is why, after

00:06:36.230 --> 00:06:40.850
appearing as Babydoll's pseudo-spirit guide
in Sucker Punch, he's since gone on to play

00:06:40.850 --> 00:06:46.350
virtually the same role in the Netflix series
Daredevil, only minus his eyesight and plus

00:06:46.350 --> 00:06:48.300
a very big stick.

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:51.410
Glenn is as tough off-screen as the characters
he plays.

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:56.550
The dude is approaching 80 and still trains
with Seal Team 6 to stay in shape for his

00:06:56.550 --> 00:06:57.550
roles.

00:06:57.550 --> 00:07:01.639
And when he's not making a movie or TV show,
he's a die-hard thrill-seeker.

00:07:01.639 --> 00:07:05.990
If he's not on camera, you'll probably find
him riding motorcycles, jumping out of planes,

00:07:05.990 --> 00:07:08.990
or spear-fishing in the middle of the open
ocean.

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:12.700
When you're beating up fish with your bare
hands, you know you've made it.

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:18.900
Thanks for watching!

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:21.860
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:21.860 --> 00:07:24.610
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

